WEBVTT

00:00:00.525 --> 00:00:03.929
Journey twenty-one: share or report a listing.

00:00:03.929 --> 00:00:08.961
Anyone can pass a listing on, and a member can privately report one.

00:00:08.961 --> 00:00:13.845
This run takes the journey from seventy-eight percent to complete.

00:00:14.699 --> 00:00:18.810
Anyone, signed in or not, presses Share on a listing.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:24.240
The dialog, Share Luzandre dot com, shows the listing's own link, with

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.723
Copy, E-mail, WhatsApp and More.

00:00:27.425 --> 00:00:32.643
Copy puts the link on the clipboard. The button reads Copied for two

00:00:32.643 --> 00:00:37.554
seconds, and a polite status tells a screen reader: Link copied.

00:00:37.554 --> 00:00:39.473
Focus stays where it was.

00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:45.554
More appears only where the device has a share sheet, and opens it with

00:00:45.554 --> 00:00:49.343
the name and the link. Both cases now have a test.

00:00:50.045 --> 00:00:55.316
Done closes the dialog, and focus returns to Share, the control that

00:00:55.316 --> 00:00:57.797
opened it. Escape does the same.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.555
A pasted link builds a preview in a chat.

00:01:01.555 --> 00:01:06.812
This is the image every shared listing now carries: the Jubilee lockup,

00:01:06.812 --> 00:01:08.960
drawn from the design tokens.

00:01:09.818 --> 00:01:14.483
The app's host now tells a link-preview fetcher from a browser.

00:01:14.483 --> 00:01:19.297
WhatsApp, Facebook, Slack and the others get the business's name,

00:01:19.297 --> 00:01:22.778
tagline and that image. A browser gets the app.

00:01:23.756 --> 00:01:28.979
Reporting needs an account. A visitor who presses Report this listing is

00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:33.404
asked to join or sign in first, and comes back to the report.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:39.076
Joanna, signed in, opens the report. Reports are private.

00:01:39.076 --> 00:01:44.767
She chooses: the listing is misleading or out of date, and writes a

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:48.250
sentence. The counter shows what is left.

00:01:48.953 --> 00:01:52.596
On its way, the form is read-only and busy.

00:01:52.596 --> 00:01:55.985
A second press, or Escape, does nothing.

00:01:56.686 --> 00:02:00.006
The server answers, and the dialog thanks her.

00:02:00.006 --> 00:02:05.059
Her report is private, and the verification team reviews it within one

00:02:05.059 --> 00:02:05.998
business day.

00:02:08.146 --> 00:02:13.077
In the same transaction as the report, the team is e-mailed: New report,

00:02:13.077 --> 00:02:17.735
with the business, the reason, what happened and a link to it in the

00:02:17.735 --> 00:02:20.338
admin application. Never the reporter.

00:02:21.196 --> 00:02:26.271
Tests prove each criterion: the share sheet, the announcement, focus,

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:30.611
the busy dialog, and a report that fails after ten seconds.

00:02:30.611 --> 00:02:34.804
API tests prove the e-mail; host tests prove the preview.

00:02:35.665 --> 00:02:40.971
Journey twenty-one is complete, with no migration and no new setting.

00:02:40.971 --> 00:02:46.201
Left for the owner: the visual, responsive and accessibility sweeps.
